| Study Period (years)  | Requirements  | Entrance Test Materials\nAutomotive and Robotics Engineering  | S1  | 4 – 5  | SMA (Science) / SMA (Social)* /  SMK* / Kurikulum Merdeka*  | Study Skill, Logic, Abstraction Non Verbal & Verbal Test\nProduct Design Engineering\nBusiness Engineering\n\n*For SMA (Social), SMK and Kurikulum Merdeka details, please contact:\n\nBINUS ASO Admissions\n021 – 53 69 69 69 ext. 6608\nWhatsapp : 0811 961 8453\n\nBINUS ASO School Of Engineering\n\nBINUS UNIVERSITY\n\n⁦BINUS @BSD Kawasan Ekonomi Khusus Edukasi, Teknologi dan Kesehatan Internasional Banten (KEK ETKI Banten), Digital Hub Kav. N 11-16, Sampora, Kec. Cisauk, Kabupaten Tangerang, Banten 15345⁩\n\nPhone\n\nPhone +6221 - 53696969 ext. 6608 & 0811 961 8453 (WA)--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDistribution of School Dropouts in Indonesian Provinces for the 2025/2026 Academic Year (https://databoks.katadata.co.id/en/education/statistics/6a0bb7b02083a/distribution-of-school-dropouts-in-indonesian-provinces-for-the-20252026-academic-year)\nciteturn421search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Image: The number of dropouts in Indonesia by province and level of education (School Year 2025/2026) ...   * #High School (SMA)\n\n# Distribution of School Dropouts in Indonesian Provinces for the 2025/2026 Academic Year\n\nImage: 1\n\nAkbar Ridwan 19/05/2026 17:46 WIB\n\nAccording to a report from the Ministry of Basic and Secondary Education (Kemendikdasmen), there were 58,623 Indonesian students who dropped out of school in the 2025/2026 academic year.\n\nImage: The number of dropouts in Indonesia by province and level of education (School Year 2025/2026)\n\n  * A Small Font\n\nAccording to a report from the Ministry of Basic and Secondary Education (Kemendikdasmen), there were 58,623 Indonesian students who dropped out of school in the 2025/2026 academic year.\n\nThis figure includes students who dropped out of high school (6,273), vocational schools (8,807), junior high schools (10,088), elementary schools (32,849), and special education schools (606) both in public and private schools.\n\nThis data is sourced from the Education Master Data (Dapodik) as of November 30, 2025, managed by Kemendikdasmen, and has undergone a verification and validation process.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSingapore Medical Association - For Doctors, For Patients (https://www.sma.org.sg/news/2026/May/2026-SMA-Annual-General-Meeting)\nciteturn421search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Crawled: last month; Members were referred to the SMA Annual Report 2025/2026 themed \"A United Voice for the Profession\", which was then adopted. ... SMACF awarded bursaries to 46 medical students in the academic year 2025/2026, disbursing a total of $276K.\n\n# 2026 SMA Annual General Meeting\n\nLee Sze Yong\n\nDr Daniel Lee Hsien Chieh was elected as SMA President during the SMA Annual General Meeting (AGM) held on 26 April 2026 in a hybrid format.\n\nOutgoing President Dr Ng Chee Kwan started the proceedings by thanking Members for attending the AGM either in-person or via teleconference.\n\nOutgoing Honorary Secretary Clinical Asst Prof Benny Loo Kai Guo highlighted the ground rules for the AGM and led the review of the 2025 AGM minutes. The minutes were confirmed and adopted, with a minor administrative amendment and no matters arising.\n\nMembers were referred to the SMA Annual Report 2025/2026 themed \"A United Voice for the Profession\", which was then adopted.\n\nHaving achieved quorum at the AGM, Members voted on nine proposed amendments to the constitution.\n\nVoting was conducted using the Zoom poll function for both online and physical attendees, with physical voting slips as a backup for physical attendees who were unable to vote with Zoom.\n\nAll the amendments were passed with the required two-thirds majority. ----------------------